  "steps": [
    "Preheat the oven to 350°F. Grease a deep-dish pie plate or 8-inch baking dish with butter or cooking spray.",
    "In a large bowl, combine the apples, sugar, cinnamon, lemon juice, vanilla, and cornstarch (if using). Toss until evenly coated, then pour into the prepared dish.",
    "In a separate bowl, combine the flour, oats, brown sugar, salt, and a pinch of cinnamon. Pour in the melted butter and stir until crumbly.",
    "Sprinkle the topping evenly over the apples.",
    "Bake 45 to 60 minutes, until the fruit is tender and the topping is golden brown.",
    "Cool slightly, drizzle with caramel sauce, and serve warm with vanilla ice cream or whipped cream."
